R"VG(
# industrial.vg (H-04; the second pass 2026-10-10): the newspaper of the industrial and the modern ages (printed pages): its masthead (the
# people's own: its name, its motto, its price in their coin), the news in the news's register (news*.vg), then the columns of a town's
# paper (industrial3.vg: the market, the council, the courts, the letters, the hall, the sport, the shipping, the railway) and its
# advertisements (industrial4.vg). The ledger, the report, the patent, the telegrams and the factory's rules are industrial5.vg's; the
# census, the timetable, the obituary industrial2.vg's; the voice on a wax cylinder industrial6.vg's.

@root patent.*

# ---- the newspaper ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

genre.newspaper (words=45..235)
  {paper.mast}\n{@digest public news 2}\n{ind.col} {ind.col}\n{ind.ads}
  {paper.mast}\n{@digest public news 3}\n{ind.col}\n{ind.ads}
  {paper.mast}\n{@digest public news 1}\n{ind.col} {ind.col} {ind.col}\n{ind.ads}
  {paper.mast}\n{@digest public news 2}\n{ind.col}\n{ind.col} {ind.col}\n{ind.ads}
  (age>=modern) {paper.mast}\n{@digest public news 2}\n{ind.col.m} {ind.col}\n{ind.ads}
  (age>=modern) {paper.mast}\n{@digest public news 3}\n{ind.col.m}\n{ind.ads}

# the masthead: the paper's name (the history's gazette where it founded one), the date, the price, now and then a motto
paper.mast (formula)
  (has:gazette) {gazette}. {paper.date}. Price {paper.price}.
  (has:gazette) {gazette}, {paper.date}. {paper.motto}.
  (!has:gazette) The {city} {ind.paper.name}. {paper.date}.
  (!has:gazette) The {$home} {ind.paper.name}. {paper.date}. {paper.when}.
  (!has:gazette) The {$home} {ind.paper.name}: {paper.motto}. {paper.date}. Price {paper.price}.
  The {city} {ind.paper.name}, {paper.date}. Price {paper.price}.
  (has:gazette) {gazette}, the {#year:ord} year of {city}, {season.now} edition.
  (age>=modern) The {$home} {ind.paper.name}. {paper.date}. {paper.when}.

paper.date
  the {#year:ord} year of {city}, {season.now}
  year {#year:digits}, {season.now}
  {season.now}, the year {#year:digits}
  the {#year:ord} year, {season.now}

paper.price
  one {smallcoin}
  two {smallcoin}
  {n} {smallcoin}
  (age>=modern) {n} {coin}

paper.when
  Published every morning except the rest day
  Every evening, and twice on market days
  Weekly, on the eve of the rest day
  Read in every house from {city} to the sea
  (age>=modern) Morning and evening editions

ind.paper.name (people=2)
  Herald
  Courier
  Chronicle
  Messenger
  Post
  Advertiser
  Intelligencer
  Mirror
  Tribune
  Lamp
  Bell
  Record
  Observer
  Bulletin
  Citizen
  Weekly
  Lantern
  Sentinel
  Clarion

paper.motto (people=1)
  What happened, and what it cost
  Truth, and the market prices
  Without fear, and without much money
  For the {crop} country
  Founded by subscription, and still owing
  The news before it is old
  Read aloud in every kitchen
  Fair to all, and kind to the dead
  Every word paid for
  The town's own paper
  Plain news for plain people
  Ink and the truth
  Under {skyone}, the news
  No master but the reader

# ---- the modern paper's own columns ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ind.col.m
  (once inv.radio=1) {ind.radio}
  (once) {ind.traffic}
  (once) {ind.cinema}
  (once inv.telephone=1) {ind.phone}
  (once) {ind.shares}
  (once) {ind.forecast}

ind.radio
  Tonight on the wireless: {ind.radio.what}, and the late news at the [usual hour|hour after|close].
  The wireless {ind.radio.what2}; the listeners' letters on the subject are printed on the next page.
ind.radio.what
  a concert of {instrument} music from the hall at {city}
  a talk on {craft} for beginners
  the {ind.sport} from {city2}, described by a man who has never played
  a play about the founding of {city}
  readings from the old songs
  the farming hour, with the price of {crop}
ind.radio.what2
  will carry the {festival} service from {holyplace} this year
  is to broadcast the council's sittings, which nobody asked for
  has a new announcer, and everyone has an opinion about her voice
  will be silent on the rest day by order

ind.traffic
  (age>=modern) {streets.of} of {$home} were blocked for an hour yesterday by [a broken cart and the people watching it|the {herd} going to the market|a parade nobody had been told of|the queue for the new {food} shop].
  (age>=modern) The crossing at {town.open} is to have a policeman [at the busy hours|from first light|on market days], after a third accident {season.this}.

ind.cinema
  At the picture hall this week: {ind.film}, [twice nightly|at the late show only|with music].
  The picture hall at {$home} will close for repairs; its seats [are older than the films|have been complained of since it opened|are to be sold].
ind.film
  a film about the founding of {city}
  a comedy about an apprentice in the {craft} trade
  the drama of the great flood
  a film of the {festival} procession, in which many of our readers may find themselves
  a story of the old wars, very loud

ind.phone
  The telephone exchange at {$home} will add [two hundred|five hundred|a thousand] lines by {season.next}; those waiting are asked to go on waiting.
  Calls to {city} will be cheaper after dark from the first of the month.

ind.shares
  The exchange: {ind.share.a}, {ind.share.b}.
  On the exchange yesterday {ind.share.a}; {ind.share.b}.
ind.share.a
  the {craft} companies rose
  {crop} fell on talk of a good harvest
  the railway shares were steady
  shipping rose on the news from the coast
  the mines fell again
ind.share.b
  and nobody could say why
  the dealers went home early
  {city2} followed {city}, as it always does
  a fortune was made by someone, and lost by someone else

ind.forecast
  Tomorrow: {weather.now}, {ind.fc.tail}.
  The forecast for {$home}: {weather.now} in the morning, {ind.fc.tail}.
ind.fc.tail
  clearing later
  and more of it
  worse in the hills
  with the {bird} flying low, which our readers will know means rain
  then whatever the sky decides
)VG"
